        "content": "## Developer Overview – FOI Backend API Manager\n\n**Purpose:**\nShared gateway for every call the FOI n8n workflows make to the FOI request-management API. Callers pass a `category` and this workflow makes the matching authenticated REST call.\n\n**Trigger/Entry:**\nSub-workflow only. Inputs: `category`, `rawRequestId`, `foiRequestId`, `ministryRequestId`, `rawReqPayload`, `reqPayload`, `servicekey`, `saveDataPayload`, `eventId`, and (for `foi-event-ack` only) the optional `eventStatus` (default COMPLETED; FOI Error Handler sends FAILED), `eventError` and `eventExecutionId`.\n\n**Processing:**\nMaps the inputs and the API base URL (`foi_api_url`), gets a bearer token from FOI OIDC, then `Category Router` picks one HTTP call (each retries up to 3 times).\n\n**Integration/Outcome:**\nCategories: `payonline` (payment details), `foipayment-save`, `foipayment-cancel`, `foipayment-get` (latest payment version, read-only), `foiemail`, `foiemail-ack`, `foinotifications-expiry`, `foi-cache-refresh`, `foi-duedate-reminder`, `foi-event-ack`, `foipayment-formsubmission-create` (POST, `reqPayload` `{formType: payonline | payoutstanding}`, returns `formId`, `submissionId`, `paymentUrl`; never retried because each call makes a new submission), `foipayment-formsubmission-update` (PATCH, `reqPayload` `{formId, submissionId, paymentStatus: PAID | CANCELLED, status?}`). Returns the API response to the caller. An unknown category stops with an error.",
        "height": 568,
        "width": 620,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "0fe85048-62e5-4708-952a-91fe42a9ac91",
      "name": "Developer Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1712,
        208
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "PUT",
        "url": "={{ $('Set Process Variables').item.json.foi_api_url }}/api/foiworkflow/events/{{ $('Set Process Variables').first().json.eventId }}",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            },
            {
              "name": "Authorization",
              "value": "=Bearer {{ $json.access_token }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "sendBody": true,
        "contentType": "raw",
        "rawContentType": "application/json",
        "body": "={{ JSON.stringify({ status: $('Set Process Variables').first().json.eventStatus || 'COMPLETED', executionid: $('Set Process Variables').first().json.eventExecutionId || $execution.id, error: $('Set Process Variables').first().json.eventError || undefined }) }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "e836a646-8438-49b6-a0f0-04d0a93ec5fa",
      "name": "Acknowledge: Outcome",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.4,
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 3,
      "waitBetweenTries": 2000,
      "position": [
        0,
        1536
      ],
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
      "notes": "Reports the outcome to the API outbox. Default is COMPLETED (DELIVERED -> COMPLETED), called by FOI Request Routing. FOI Error Handler passes eventStatus=FAILED, eventError and the failed run's id (DELIVERED -> FAILED). Idempotent PUT, so retry is safe. Also runs for skipped duplicates so a replayed event that had already completed is closed. A failure here is not a business failure: it continues, and the API sweeper flags an event with no outcome."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $('Set Process Variables').item.json.foi_api_url }}/api/foiworkflow/events/{{ $('Set Process Variables').first().json.eventId }}/claim",
